Daiane,

I deployed a fix so you should be able to use the seasonal package without having to set the X13_PATH variable. Let me know if this works.

-Andy

On Wed, Jul 1, 2015 at 1:13 PM, Andy Kipp <an...@rstudio.com> wrote:
> Daiane,
>
> The /opt/x13as option will ONLY work on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>, I am going to fix the other bug and then you should be able to use seasonal without having to set the X13_PATH at all. So it should work locally and on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>.
>
> I will send other update when I've fixed the issue.
> -Andy
>
> On Wed, Jul 1, 2015 at 1:06 PM, Daiane Mattos <daimm...@gmail.com> wrote:
> > Andy,
> > I was trying Sys.setenv(X13_PATH = '/data/x13as') and putting the X13 executable file there instead of Sys.setenv(X13_PATH = '/opt/x13as').
> >
> > I did not know this option '/ opt / x13as'.
> > It worked very well.
> > Thank you very much for your attention !!
> > :D
> >
> > Em quarta-feira, 1 de julho de 2015 11:33:55 UTC-3, Andy Kipp escreveu:
> > > Daiane,
> > >
> > > It looks like there may be another issue. I'm looking into that now.
> > >
> > > As a workaround can you try this:
> > >
> > > Sys.setenv(X13_PATH = '/opt/x13as')
