Welcome to R.  It is probably rough to get started by looking at someone else's application.  I would strongly encourage you to take a look at the tutorial and some of the articles at:  shiny.rstudio.com <http://shiny.rstudio.com> .  The tutorial will take you a couple of hours to get through, you could also watch a three part webinar we have posted here <https://www.rstudio.com/resources/webinars/> that will walk you through how Shiny works.  You don't really knit a shiny application.  You can run it by typing runApp() in the directory that has your app.R or your ui.R and server.R files.

The discussion list that you will find particularly helpful for asking shiny related questions is the shiny-discuss list <https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/shiny-discuss> which provides support for what shiny is and how to use it.  shinyapps-users is a discussion list that is focused on helping people who are trying to deploy their shiny applications to the shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> cloud.

Best of luck,
Tareef

